Subject: [PATCH 7/7] grate: assign alternating raster swaths on Tegra30

The common initialization broadcasts zero to HORIZONTAL_SWATH_RENDERING
on both pixel pipelines. Configure alternating horizontal swaths separately
for GPU A (value 1, even) and GPU B (value 3, odd), then restore broadcast
register writes. This matches libgrate's Tegra30 draw setup.

With the cache invalidation and synchronous submission corrections applied,
this removes the measured wrong-face-colour streaks inside solid faces in
rotating depth-tested cube captures. No application culling, omitted faces,
depth disablement or forced-submit-wait environment variable is needed.

Applies after 0006 on grate-26.2.3. Limited to Tegra30; remaining silhouette
pixel differences from software rendering are not claimed fixed.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
@@ -382,6 +382,19 @@
       UNREACHABLE("invalid index_size");
    }
 
+   /* Tegra30 has two pixel pipelines. Assign alternating horizontal swaths
+    * to GPU A (even) and GPU B (odd), as in libgrate's draw setup. Leaving
+    * both at the common reset value can corrupt depth-tested face interiors.
+    * Restore broadcast writes before emitting the remaining draw state.
+    */
+   if (context->drm->soc_id == DRM_TEGRA_SOC_T30) {
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_GSHIM_WRITE_MASK, 1));
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_GLOBAL_HORIZONTAL_SWATH_RENDERING, 1));
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_GSHIM_WRITE_MASK, 2));
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_GLOBAL_HORIZONTAL_SWATH_RENDERING, 3));
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_GSHIM_WRITE_MASK, 3));
+   }
+
    /* draw params */
    value  = TGR3D_IDX_SET_PRIM_DRAW_MODE(index_size);
    value |= context->rast->draw_params;
